Design Document for pstty
-----------------------------------------------------------
Code by: Zachary Weed 
-----------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:

  pstty (partial stty) is used for defining configuration settings on a terminal device

Outline:

  pstty works by using ioctl(), tcsetattr(), tcgetattr(), and the termios struct as a 
  means of both displaying and configuring the current teletype (tty) device. While it
  does not yet support all of the flags in many *nix systems, only supporing: erase, kill,
  intr, echo, isig, igncr, parodd, min, and time, thus far. We accomplish this through 
  storing the state of each of the values in a struct, and associating a function pointer
  member with the structs, that provides a simple way of modifying the values, without
  iterating through all of the flags individually and explicitly.

